":"https://api.github.com/users/LeLeLeonid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeLeLeonid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeLeLeonid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeLeLeonid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeLeLeonid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeLeLeonid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T05:22:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T05:22:33Z","body":"Hey guys, just wanted to share something weird. I tested 4.4.1 on my old graphics card and here's what I found:\r\nGot an old NVIDIA GTX 650 Ti (Kepler) running on Windows 10. On Godot 4.4 stable, Vulkan (Forward+/Mobile) worked totally fine, no issues. But when I updated to 4.4.1 stable, boom! Instant crash whenever I try to use Vulkan. Editor just dies. If I force it to use OpenGL (`--rendering-driver opengl3`), then it runs okay.\r\n\r\nSo yeah, seems like something in 4.4.1 broke Vulkan specifically for this older card. Since 4.4 was good and this PR #104592 messed with Vulkan init stuff, maybe it's related? Dunno, just thought I'd let you know in case it helps track down a bug. Cheers!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800504669/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2801779663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104592#issuecomment-2801779663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104592","id":2801779663,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m_8PP","user":{"login":"unvermuthet","id":40361609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzYxNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40361609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url"